PATCH 526: the c33c display-list phase handlers 5fb0 / 6016 and their record builder 66f2.

FOUR of the nine remaining self-play SIGSEGVs -- INDIA2 (t=5801), INDIA5 (t=1988), TRAIN3 (t=9515),
TRAIN4 (t=835) -- crash at the SAME instruction with the SAME arguments:

    #0 FUN_1000_66f2 (param_1=20, param_2=0x0, param_3=265604)
    #1 FUN_0000_5fb0 (param_1=0x40d84)
    #2 FUN_0000_c33c (si=0, di=27582)          <- the patch-310 render-record iterator
    #3 FUN_0000_378e  #4 FUN_0000_22dd  #5 FUN_0000_459a

c33c walks a 10-entry phase-handler table at DGROUP:0xe6f5 and calls each handler through
`call *[bx+0xe6f5]` with NO arguments, keeping the ES:DI record cursor in g_fist_render_di (patch 310)
and the handler's CF verdict in g_fist_cf (patch 463).  5fb0 is handler idx 2 and 6016 its sibling;
both were left pristine, so Ghidra's invented `param_1` (0x40d84 -- whatever happened to be in the
register) was used as the destination pointer and every DGROUP near offset in the pair was
dereferenced as a host address.

asm-verified against re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:

  0x166f2 (= 0f69:0x7062, the builder called by 5fb0)
      add di,2 / mov ax,si; stosw / mov bx,cx; stosw / add di,2 / mov ax,0; stosw
      mov eax,[si]; stosd / mov eax,[si+4]; stosd; stosd / xor ax,ax; stosw x4 / add di,0x14 / lret
    -> ES:DI destination (ES = DGROUP, the patch-310 cursor), DS:SI source (si = word[0x7d20], a
       DGROUP near offset), and DI = entry+0x32 on return -- all three dropped.

  0x5fb0 (handler idx 2)
      testb [0x7d1c],0xff; jne 6014            ; stc = phase finished
      si=[0x7d20]; al=0x14; ah=byte[0x7d1d]; lcall 0f69:7062
      ax=[0x7d22]; stosw / ax=[0x7d20]; stosw / [0x7d22]=ax
      bx=[0x7c04]; mov gs,[0x70]; mov gs:[bx+0x12c7],ax
      addw [0x7c04],2 / addw [0x7d20],8 / decw [0x7d1e]; jne 6012
      incw [0x7d24] / decw [0x7d26] / cmpw [0x7d26],4; jne 6003 / al=[0x7d29]; [0x7d28]=al
      lcall 0f69:708b (= 671b) / jae 6012 / si=0xffff; movb [0x7d1c],0xff
      6012: clc; ret        6014: stc; ret
    -> the two stosw's land at the DI 66f2 left behind, not at param_1+0/+2; the `mov gs,[0x70]`
       STRSEG base on the [bx+0x12c7] ring slot was dropped (the 8463/9ab5 GS class); and Ghidra
       synthesised `bVar1 = DAT_2000_3d26 < 4` from the `cmpw` -- the CF the `jae` tests is the one
       671b RETURNS (patch 292 publishes it in g_fist_cf), and `jae` skips on CF=0, so the
       phase-finished flag is set when CF=1, i.e. when 671b reports the cell list exhausted.

  0x6016 (the sibling that replays the ring 5fb0 fills; the next SIGSEGV once 5fb0 stops crashing)
      bx=[0x7c06]; cmp bx,[0x7c04]; jae 6051   ; stc = ring drained
      mov gs,[0x70]; mov si,gs:[bx+0x12c7]
      add di,2; xor ax,ax; stosw / al=0x10,ah=0; stosw; stosw; stosw
      mov eax,[si]; stosd / mov eax,[si+4]; stosd; stosd / add di,0x1c / ax=0x13a8; stosw
      addw [0x7c06],2; clc; ret
    -> same three defects; DI = entry+0x34 on return.

The GS reconstruction follows patch 229's idiom: STRSEG = word[DGROUP:0x70], base g_mem+(STRSEG<<4),
16-bit effective offset (bx+0x12c7).

ALSO in this patch: FUN_0000_38aa (asm 0x38aa-0x390b), the render method 378e dispatches on the records
5fb0/6016 build -- with the builders fixed it becomes the very next SIGSEGV in all four missions, at the
same tick and in the same frame, so it belongs to the same surface.  Its four defects (object near-offset
deref'd as a host pointer, 3d4c's dropped CX output substituted by the incoming cx, int*-scaled viewport
field reads, and the dropped AL/BX arguments to the [0x648]/[0x654] far vector) are documented at the
site.

